From 45c1e518adb851a4377fda852b94410622cc57a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emberloom-godot <emberloom-godot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:30:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Add Vulkan low latency: VK_AMD_anti_lag and
 VK_NV_low_latency2

RenderingDevice.low_latency_is_supported / set_enabled / is_enabled and
low_latency_get_input_to_present_usec. The OS main loop (Linux/BSD, Windows)
raises an input marker before process_events (Anti-Lag input stage, NV latency
sleep + simulation start + input sample), the RD compositor a render-start
marker (simulation end + render submit start), and the Vulkan present path the
present stage (Anti-Lag present, NV render submit end / present start / end +
VkPresentIdKHR). Extensions are requested through the extra device extensions
project setting; NV needs VK_KHR_present_id and timeline semaphores. Off by
default; unsupported devices and other drivers keep no-op defaults.
---
 doc/classes/RenderingDevice.xml               |  25 ++
 .../vulkan/rendering_device_driver_vulkan.cpp | 247 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../vulkan/rendering_device_driver_vulkan.h   |  30 +++
 platform/linuxbsd/os_linuxbsd.cpp             |   5 +
 platform/windows/os_windows.cpp               |   5 +
 .../renderer_rd/renderer_compositor_rd.cpp    |   2 +
 servers/rendering/rendering_device.cpp        |  43 +++
 servers/rendering/rendering_device.h          |  17 ++
 servers/rendering/rendering_device_driver.h   |  10 +
 9 files changed, 384 insertions(+)

